    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x)=x^2+\\dfrac{b}{a}x+\\dfrac{c}{a}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f'(x)=2x+\\dfrac{b}{a}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{(x+h)^2+\\frac{b}{a}(x+h)+\\frac{c}{a}-\\left(x^2+\\frac{b}{a}x+\\frac{c}{a}\\right)}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{2xh+h^2+\\frac{b}{a}h}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\left(2x+h+\\frac{b}{a}\\right)\\\\f'(x)&=2x+\\frac{b}{a}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
